@* Alternate for the Page content type (terms, privacy, disclaimer, ...). Orchard's default
   Content.cshtml renders the zones into a bare <article>, which under Tailwind's Preflight means the
   TitlePart <h1> and the raw HtmlBodyPart markup arrive with no margins and no heading sizes. Wrapping
   the zones in `prose` gives that HTML its rhythm back, using the theme's own tokens (see site.css), so
   these pages sit inside the site design without anyone having to touch the content.

   The zones are rendered rather than the parts individually, so whatever a Page carries now or later
   (title, body, anything added in the admin) is picked up. `max-w-3xl` on the same element overrides
   prose's default 65ch measure. *@
<article class="bg-white">
    @* Not `band` (the marketing sections' clamp(5rem,10vw,9rem) rhythm) — that leaves a ~144px hole
       above the title on a document page. *@
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-1 pt-12 pb-20">
        <div class="prose prose-lg mx-auto max-w-3xl">
            @await DisplayAsync(Model.Header)
            @await DisplayAsync(Model.Content)
            @await DisplayAsync(Model.Footer)
        </div>
    </div>
</article>
